            "text": "  rule #fixSpacesBody\n    => Assign(Name(\"result\"), Str(\"\"))\n       Assign(Name(\"spaces\"), Str(\"\"))\n       Assign(Name(\"char\"), Str(\"\"))\n       For(Name(\"char\"), Name(\"text\"), #fixSpacesLoopBody)\n       Return(BinOp(\"+\", Name(\"result\"), Name(\"spaces\")))"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 36,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "14a4162ef746a7b1514f1437363b58b37917f4d4e3d88fefed3c57ad2805fc1c",
            "rationale": "This is the guarded defining case of pendingSpace for the two-underscore encoding, mapping the next space to the saturated dash encoding.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-14a4162ef746a7b1514f1437363b58b37917f4d4e3d88fefed3c57ad2805fc1c",
            "start_line": 34,
            "text": "  rule pendingSpace(P:IntSeq)\n    => iCons(45, .IntSeq)\n    requires P ==K iCons(95, iCons(95, .IntSeq))"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 40,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "3a1617f33a2052cf0e47d921ef5d9d446c818e4e28613c67cb7e98fd12477ce5",
            "rationale": "This is the guarded defining case of pendingSpace that keeps an already saturated dash encoding unchanged.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-3a1617f33a2052cf0e47d921ef5d9d446c818e4e28613c67cb7e98fd12477ce5",
            "start_line": 37,
            "text": "  rule pendingSpace(P:IntSeq)\n    => P\n    requires P ==K iCons(45, .IntSeq)\n     andBool notBool (P ==K iCons(95, iCons(95, .IntSeq)))"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 44,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "4a9240ff48e39b4f7ca7cdf130ac4cc929faa5a1db52064fce7d072847973398",
            "rationale": "This is the remaining guarded defining case of pendingSpace, appending one underscore when the pending encoding is neither two underscores nor a dash.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-4a9240ff48e39b4f7ca7cdf130ac4cc929faa5a1db52064fce7d072847973398",
            "start_line": 41,
            "text": "  rule pendingSpace(P:IntSeq)\n    => seqConcat(P, iCons(95, .IntSeq))\n    requires notBool (P ==K iCons(95, iCons(95, .IntSeq)))\n     andBool notBool (P ==K iCons(45, .IntSeq))"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 48,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "cb3f7e78e89867dea79ff1da3d0ba357a2f19ba166a3105d0bfb180249bcef15",
            "rationale": "This base equation defines resultAfter on an empty remaining character sequence as the current completed result.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-cb3f7e78e89867dea79ff1da3d0ba357a2f19ba166a3105d0bfb180249bcef15",
            "start_line": 48,
            "text": "  rule resultAfter(.IntSeq, R:IntSeq, _P:IntSeq) => R"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 50,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "ab4d5becfd8d470f186d1f245d2ab65f5bf113c326562df2b5ed37d0ab7ad93f",
            "rationale": "This recurrence defines resultAfter for a leading space by consuming that character, preserving the completed result, and updating the pending-space summary.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-ab4d5becfd8d470f186d1f245d2ab65f5bf113c326562df2b5ed37d0ab7ad93f",
            "start_line": 49,
            "text": "  rule resultAfter(iCons(32, CS:IntSeq), R:IntSeq, P:IntSeq)\n    => resultAfter(CS, R, pendingSpace(P))"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [
                "simplification"
            ],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 57,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "2474ff592cce4297eb234f57f5266cadd5c79784f4555511da449c9dc39aecd8",
            "rationale": "Although marked simplification, this is the guarded non-space recurrence that defines resultAfter by consuming one character, flushing the pending encoding, and resetting it; it is not an independent lemma.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-2474ff592cce4297eb234f57f5266cadd5c79784f4555511da449c9dc39aecd8",
            "start_line": 51,
            "text": "  rule resultAfter(iCons(C:Int, CS:IntSeq), R:IntSeq, P:IntSeq)\n    => resultAfter(\n         CS,\n         seqConcat(R, seqConcat(P, iCons(C, .IntSeq))),\n         .IntSeq)\n    requires C =/=Int 32\n    [simplification]"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 60,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "914d02541b0edb3ef3039272a8847fb5d5859793d3bc8e6b5d81637111b9ec0f",
            "rationale": "This base equation defines pendingAfter on an empty remaining sequence as the current pending-space encoding.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-914d02541b0edb3ef3039272a8847fb5d5859793d3bc8e6b5d81637111b9ec0f",
            "start_line": 60,
            "text": "  rule pendingAfter(.IntSeq, P:IntSeq) => P"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 62,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "abb763d32b8c0b7f1f499857f237890d9e7325671320addc7babf2323b088c8b",
            "rationale": "This recurrence defines pendingAfter for a leading space by consuming the character and applying the pendingSpace state transition.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-abb763d32b8c0b7f1f499857f237890d9e7325671320addc7babf2323b088c8b",
            "start_line": 61,
            "text": "  rule pendingAfter(iCons(32, CS:IntSeq), P:IntSeq)\n    => pendingAfter(CS, pendingSpace(P))"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [
                "simplification"
            ],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 66,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "38a7a54771406f0fcf4f53d56873c51b354f06859365120b1441f6bd9ad3b4a8",
            "rationale": "Although marked simplification, this is the guarded non-space recurrence that defines pendingAfter by consuming one character and resetting the pending encoding; it is not an independent lemma.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-38a7a54771406f0fcf4f53d56873c51b354f06859365120b1441f6bd9ad3b4a8",
            "start_line": 63,
            "text": "  rule pendingAfter(iCons(C:Int, CS:IntSeq), _P:IntSeq)\n    => pendingAfter(CS, .IntSeq)\n    requires C =/=Int 32\n    [simplification]"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 69,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "a1cc403dbcce337ddeafd5bfaaf336abab04bc666cabf437ea542f2b3720af14",
            "rationale": "This base equation defines charAfter on an empty remaining sequence as the existing loop-target value.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-a1cc403dbcce337ddeafd5bfaaf336abab04bc666cabf437ea542f2b3720af14",
            "start_line": 69,
            "text": "  rule charAfter(.IntSeq, CH:Val) => CH"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 71,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "9c34344a0ea1cb0299269885158d8750178870205348fe7c9d6179fad345aa02",
            "rationale": "This recurrence defines charAfter by consuming one code and recording its one-character string as the latest loop-target value.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-9c34344a0ea1cb0299269885158d8750178870205348fe7c9d6179fad345aa02",
            "start_line": 70,
            "text": "  rule charAfter(iCons(C:Int, CS:IntSeq), _CH:Val)\n    => charAfter(CS, str(iCons(C, .IntSeq)))"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 77,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "ab0ca6a8cd8575cfb385c12e545c1f7abe205f28060972c8e6873b21bee131d5",
            "rationale": "This equation defines fixedSpaces as the concatenation of the recursively defined final completed-result and pending-space summaries.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-ab0ca6a8cd8575cfb385c12e545c1f7abe205f28060972c8e6873b21bee131d5",
            "start_line": 74,
            "text": "  rule fixedSpaces(CS:IntSeq)\n    => seqConcat(\n         resultAfter(CS, .IntSeq, .IntSeq),\n         pendingAfter(CS, .IntSeq))"
        }
    ],
